# llvm -- packaged for mesa, not for its compilers.
#
# llvmpipe compiles GLSL shaders to machine code through LLVM at runtime. The
# alternative software rasteriser, softpipe, is an interpreter: it renders the
# same pixels perhaps an order of magnitude slower, which for GNOME Shell is the
# difference between a usable session and a slideshow. A live ISO booting in a
# virtual machine, or on hardware whose driver did not load, falls back to
# software rendering -- so this is on the critical path for exactly the case an
# ISO is most often tried in.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/releases/download/llvmorg-20.1.8/llvm-project-20.1.8.src.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=6898f963c8e938981e6c4a302e83ec5beb4630147c7311183cf61069af16333d
SRC_DIR=llvm-project-20.1.8.src
